    skos:note "Open Forest (Between 20-60% Canopy Cover) - Mainly needleleaved, evergreen, open cover of trees, with less than 60% cover, occurring mainly in mountainous areas.; Closed Forest (More Than 60% Canopy Cover) - Mainly needleleaved, evergreen, closed cover of trees, with more than 60% cover, occurring mainly in mountainous areas. Source: FAO. 1999. Provincial Land Cover Atlas of Islamic State of Afghanistan. AFG/90/002 Utilization of Remote Sensing for the Inventory and Monitoring of Agricultural Land in Afghanistan. Food and Agricultural Organization of the United Nations (FAO), United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) and Afghan Geodesy and Cartography Head Office (AGCHO). FAO, Rome"@en .

