    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "‘Forest’ is defined as dense woodland with a surface larger than 1000 m2 with a density of forest trees and shrubs not less than 30 %, which produces wood material and has influence on the surrounding environment. ‘Land with forest vegetation’ is defined as forest wood area with a density of forest trees and shrubs from 5 to 30 % which are not registered in the cadastra as other land estates. Forest estate includes also open areas up to 2 ha. such as openings, rocks and sandbank which are in forests, the surfaces occupied by forest shelterbelts, wood lots and shrub surfaces. LEX-FAOC004693. ALBANIA: Law No. 7623 for forestry and forest police service"@en .

