    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Wooded Land - Land with vegetation with a projected foliage cover of less than 10% (this is equivalent to a crown cover of 0.25 to 20%) and included Tall, Medium and Low Trees (>30, 10-30 and <10 m respectively) and Tall Shrubs (>2 m). The Tall Shrubs category excludes eucalypts as these are included under 'forest' as Mallees.\" Karol.Andrzejewski@affa.gov.au NFI (1999) definition of Other Wooded land"@en .

