    skos:note "A woody plant with a single main stem (the trunk), that is unbranched near the ground; some trees (e.g. oak, ([Quercus]) and ash ([Fraxinus])) have multi-trunked forms. At the end of each growing season there is no die-back of aerial parts, apart from the loss of foliage. Trees which are able to reach a height of 5m at maturity"@en .

