ex:Def_def_can_unknown_1549 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The establishment of trees on an area that has lacked forest cover for a very lo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Canada ;
    ex:country "Canada" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.14 STAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.1.2 Land Cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "The establishment of trees on an area that has lacked forest cover for a very long time or has never been forested. [Source: Glossary of Forestry Terms, Province of British Columbia, Ministry of Forests, via Igor A. Yakovlev] and The DELFI Vocabulary of Forest Fire Terms"@en .

ex:Def_def_can_unknown_1586 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The establishment of a tree crop on an area from which it has always or very lon..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Canada ;
    ex:country "Canada" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.14 STAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.1.3 Land Cover and Use" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "The establishment of a tree crop on an area from which it has always or very long been absent. Where such establishment fails and is repeated, the latter may properly be termed \"reafforestation\". ("@en .

ex:Def_def_can_unknown_1597 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "To clear an area of forests or trees, usually for commercial use of the lumber o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Canada ;
    ex:country "Canada" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.2 DEFORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.2.2 As a change in land cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "To clear an area of forests or trees, usually for commercial use of the lumber or agricultural use of the land"@en .

ex:Def_def_can_unknown_1632 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Clearing an area of forest on a non-temporary basis for another use. Clearcuttin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Canada ;
    ex:country "Canada" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.2 DEFORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.2.4 As a change in land cover and use" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "Clearing an area of forest on a non-temporary basis for another use. Clearcutting (even with stump removal), if shortly followed by reforestation for forestry purposes, is not deforesting. [Source: Glossary of Forestry Terms, Province of British Columbia, Ministry of Forests, via Igor A. Yakovlev]"@en .

ex:Def_def_can_unknown_1634 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Deforestation is the permanent removal of forest cover from an area, and the con..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Canada ;
    ex:country "Canada" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.2 DEFORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.2.4 As a change in land cover and use" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "Deforestation is the permanent removal of forest cover from an area, and the conversion of the previously forested land to other uses"@en .

ex:Def_def_can_unknown_1635 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Clearing an area of forest for another long-term use. ( )" ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Canada ;
