    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Congo Basin Forest Partnership. Forests are habitats where trees are dominant, where tree crowns form a more or less continuous layer and where grasses are virtually absent in the under story. The few grasses which are found in forests have broad leaves and are very different from savannah species. Forests are sensitive to fire"@en .

