ex:Def_def_ecu_2013_442 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A national forest definition was adopted ( in the context of identifying forest ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Ecuador ;
    ex:country "Ecuador" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_ecu_2013_442_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "A national forest definition was adopted ( in the context of identifying forest land in Ecuador’s land-use maps. According to this definition all land units bearing “a single minimum tree crown cover value of 30%; a single minimum land area value of 1.00 hectare; and, a single minimum tree height value of 5.00 meters” are considered as forest. This definition is consistent with Ministerial Agreement Number 033 of April the 5th, 2013 (MAE, 2013b) and with the definition of forest land used in the national greenhouse gas inventory. This definition differs from the definition applied by FAO’s Global Forest Resources Assessment (FRA 2010)"@en .

