    skos:note "Finland adopts two definitions of forests: one is the FRA FAO 2000 definition: “Forest is land spanning more than 0.5 ha with trees higher than 5 m and a canopy cover of more than 10%, or trees able to reach these 5 m thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use.” METLA (Finnish Forest Research Institute), 2009"@en .

