    skos:note "The second definition is the national definition of forest that in Finland is the same as in the two other Nordic countries, Sweden and Norway: forest is defined as a land capable of producing an annual increment of volume growing stock of at least 1 m3/ha per year over the rotation under the most favorable tree species composition, and not used for any other purpose than forestry or forestry related purposes. METLA (Finnish Forest Research Institute), 2009"@en .

