    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest: Wooden area of 50 acres with trees able to reach a height greater than five meters at maturity in situ, a of more than 10% and a width of at least 20 meters. Areas temporarily cleared or regenerating forests are classified as though they covered less than 10% during the inventory. Note: poplar (rate of free covered poplar grown on more than 75%) are included in the definition of forest. In contrast, walnut groves and chestnut groves as well as truffle cultivation and orchards are excluded (agricultural production). FN definition , new inventory method . 2009"@en .

