ex:Def_def_gre_1945_489 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "All land which has been forest or areas of equal ecological value with forest ve..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Greece ;
    ex:country "Greece" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "All land which has been forest or areas of equal ecological value with forest vegetation (like areas with wild bushes and sporadic trees with a density of their canopy ground projection larger than 25% of the area), as of 1945, is characterized as “forest” and is protected by the Law. Potsiou, Chryssy A.; Dimitriadi, Katerina. 2008. Tools for Legal Integration and Regeneration of Informal Development in Greece: A Research Study in the Municipality of Keratea. Surveying and Land Information Science 68(2): 103-118"@en .

ex:Def_def_gre_1979_1031 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Greek Constitution, article 24, “As forest or forest ecosystem is meant the orga..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Greece ;
    ex:country "Greece" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Greek Constitution, article 24, “As forest or forest ecosystem is meant the organic whole of wild plants with ligneous trunk on the requisite land surface, which, together with the co-existing flora and fauna, form throughout their mutual interdependence and interactions, a certain biological community (forest biological community) and a certain natural environment (forest environment). Wooded tract exists when in the aforementioned whole the wild ligneous vegetation, high or bushy, is sparse.”"@en .

ex:Def_def_gre_1992_866 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest Land includes: (a) areas larger than 0.5 ha or strips more than 30 m wide..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Greece ;
    ex:country "Greece" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_gre_1992_866_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_European_Union ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest Land includes: (a) areas larger than 0.5 ha or strips more than 30 m wide with tree crown cover (stand density) of more than 10% of the area, or areas with 250 trees of reproductive age per hectare, able to produce wood or other products or services and are not used for any other land-use (b) areas where trees are removed to below 10% of stand density and are not given for other landuse (c) reforested areas and (d) scrublands (areas covered by broadleaved evergreens)"@en .

