    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "NEW DEFINTION: Forest is a land with 10% crown cover with minimum height of trees of 5 m at maturity (in situ); areas of approximately 0.5 ha or strips with widths of 30 m (with tree canopy cover of 10%); areas not used for any purpose other than production of wood. Galatsidas S. 2001"@en .

