ex:Def_def_ind_2008_254 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "In India, forest area is defined by using the legal connotation. An area of land..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "In India, forest area is defined by using the legal connotation. An area of land recorded as forest in revenue records or proclaimed to be forest under a forest law or Act is described as forest”. In other words, ‘forest area’ is an area recorded as forest in the government records. This is ifferent from the ‘forest cover’ which is based on the capability of remote sensing satellite sensor and is completely independent of the legality of land use or land ownership. This data is provided by the Forest Survey of India (FSI)"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2008_524 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest cover consists of all lands having tree canopy density of more than 10 pe..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_ind_2008_524_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Forest cover consists of all lands having tree canopy density of more than 10 percent that can be interpreted from satellite data. The resolution and limitations of the sensor are crucial in estimation of area under forest cover"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2008_524_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_ind_2009_1035 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest means a unity of ecosystem in the form of land consisting of biological r..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Forest means a unity of ecosystem in the form of land consisting of biological resources dominated by trees in their natural form and environment, in which one and another are inseparable"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2009_1603 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Minister of Forestry No. 30/2009 that stated deforestation as the permanent alte..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.2 DEFORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.2.2 As a change in land cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "Minister of Forestry No. 30/2009 that stated deforestation as the permanent alteration from forested area into a non-forested area as a result of human activities (MoFor, 2009). and"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2009_255 a ex:Definition ;
