ex:Def_def_ind_unknown_531 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest area: 0.05 to 1 ha (Indonesia decided on 0.25 ha)  Potential to reach a ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_ind_unknown_531_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Forest area: 0.05 to 1 ha (Indonesia decided on 0.25 ha)  Potential to reach a minimum height at maturity in situ of 2-5 m (Indonesia decided on 5 m).  Tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level): 10 to 30 % (Indonesia decided on >30%) Under this definition a forest can contain anything from 10% to 100% tree cover; it is only when cover falls below the minimum crown cover that it designated as non-forest. However, if this is only a temporary change, such as for timber harvest with regeneration expected, the land remains in the forest classification"@en .

