    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "FOREST: It is a land mainly covered by trees, shrubs and other woody plants. Forest density is classified as follow: 1 Very dense: crown cover of woody elements (trees, shrubs) more than 75%, 2 Dense - 50 -75%, 3 Middle dense - 25 -50%, 4 Sparse 5 -25%, 5 Very - 1 - 5% \"M.Zobeiri\" <zobeiri@nrf.ut.ac.ir"@en .

