ex:Def_def_ita_1923_266 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "In Italy, forests are part of the areas submitted to restraints imposed by a 192..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Italy ;
    ex:country "Italy" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "In Italy, forests are part of the areas submitted to restraints imposed by a 1923 Italian law (R.D.L. 1923). This law obliges local authorities to demarcate all areas (not only wooded) that can not be subjected to land-use change, since they are important for slope stability, for mass and superficial erosion prevention and for regulating water regime. Regio Decreto Legislativo 30 Dicembre 1923, n. 3267. Riordinamento e riforma della legislazione in materia di boschi e terreni montani. Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it"@en .

ex:Def_def_ita_1950_1588 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(rimboschimento) - Outplanting forest stock on areas previously managed for othe..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Italy ;
    ex:country "Italy" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Vittorio_Tosi_ISAFA_Biometria_isafa ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.14 STAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.1.3 Land Cover and Use" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "(rimboschimento) - Outplanting forest stock on areas previously managed for other uses (agricultural lands, barren lands, etc.) (ISTAT). 'Imboschimento'(afforestation) is used very seldom. From: Vittorio Tosi ISAFA Biometria <isafa.biofor@tqs.it and Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it ISTAT (1950-1997). Statistiche Forestali. Annuari 1-47. Istituto Nazionale di Statistica. Rome"@en .

ex:Def_def_ita_1950_1626 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A loss of forest area because of change of land use to agricultural lands, barre..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Italy ;
    ex:country "Italy" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.2 DEFORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.2.3 As a change in land use" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "A loss of forest area because of change of land use to agricultural lands, barren lands, buildings, roads, pipelines, etc. Burned forest areas are not considered deforested. ISTAT (1950-1997). Statistiche Forestali. Annuari 1-47. Istituto Nazionale di Statistica. Rome. Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it"@en .

