    skos:note "A woody perennial plant whose cambium makes secondary growth (often includes tree ferns and bamboo). High tree : a tree with enough height ( usually more than 5m ) and with a stem readily distinguishable from branches. Low tree : a tree with a certain height limit and the general absence of a well-defined main stem. Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp"@en .

