    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "1) Land aimed at growing a group of trees (includes a non-forested land at present) or 2) a mountainous area with tree cover registered as 'forest' on a land register. Note: House lots and shrine enclosures being not aimed at growing trees are not forests even if they are covered with trees. Yukichi Konohira Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp"@en .

ex:Def_def_jap_unknown_888 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest: In this law, FOREST shall be defined as listed below. The definition, ho..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Japan ;
    ex:country "Japan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest: In this law, FOREST shall be defined as listed below. The definition, however, shall exclude lands used for agriculture, housing, or equivalent purposes and standing trees and bamboo upon those lands. (1) Lands with trees and bamboo in groups and standing tree and bamboo upon the lands. (2) Besides the lands mentioned in the paragraphs, lands that serve as habitats for trees and bamboo. Definition of Forest Law, Forest Agency. From: Masahiro Amano masahiro@ss.ffpri.affrc.go.jp"@en .

ex:Def_def_kaz_2002_1037 a ex:Definition ;
