    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "A closed stand of trees of one or more storeys, with an interlaced upper canopy, rising to 7·5-40 m or more in height. The ground cover is dominated by herbs and shrubs, and lianes and epiphytes are characteristic. Dwarf forests are as defined but rise to less than 7·5 m in height"@en .

