    ex:sectionMain "3.4 FORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.5.1 Restoration of Land Cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note ") - The installation of forest plantations on areas previously covered by forest. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg"@en .

ex:Def_def_kyr_1999_566 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "New Forest Code - One of the main types of vegetation on the Earth, comprising t..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kyrgyzstan ;
    ex:country "Kyrgyzstan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "New Forest Code - One of the main types of vegetation on the Earth, comprising trees, shrubs, grassland and other plants, including animals and microorganisms, which are biologically interrelated in their evolution and exert influence on one another and the environment. Forest soil is an integral part of the forest whole. Forest is an integral and a very important component of biosphere and geographic landscape. It plays an important role in maintaining the hydrological regime of rivers, preventing erosion and deflation of soils, combating hot dry winds. Source: Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg"@en .

ex:Def_def_kyr_2000_567 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest in strict sense (conifer/broadleaf/mixed - see definitions at 3.3) is def..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kyrgyzstan ;
    ex:country "Kyrgyzstan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_kyr_2000_567_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Forest in strict sense (conifer/broadleaf/mixed - see definitions at 3.3) is defined as vegetation consisting of forest species (according to the species list in annex 2) with the objective of timber production and various protection and other functions. The horizontal forest area has a minimum crown cover density of 20 % (see Figure 2-4, Figure 2-5 and Figure 2-6), a minimum width of 25 metres and a minimum height of 2.0 metres. In case of forest cultures no minimum height has to be considered"@en .

ex:Def_def_kyr_2000_567_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "25.0"^^xsd:float .

