ex:Def_def_kyr_unknown_1326 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A perennial plant with clearly defined stem, carrying side branches and with a t..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kyrgyzstan ;
    ex:country "Kyrgyzstan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.4.1 Definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "A perennial plant with clearly defined stem, carrying side branches and with a top shoot. The whole system of branches together with the corresponding part of the stem forms the crown. Tree is a widely spread life form of plants, playing the major role in the forest and landscape formation. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg"@en .

ex:Def_def_kyr_unknown_1670 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(from Russian it is likely to be translated as \"forest regeneration\") - The proc..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kyrgyzstan ;
    ex:country "Kyrgyzstan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.4 FORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.5.1 Restoration of Land Cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "(from Russian it is likely to be translated as \"forest regeneration\") - The process of the creation of the forest generation under the forest cover, at the fellings and forest fires sites, and other areas formerly covered with the forest. Forest regeneration can be natural, artificial and mixed. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg"@en .

ex:Def_def_kyr_unknown_565 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest -- Vegetation existing of forest species with the objective of timber pro..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kyrgyzstan ;
    ex:country "Kyrgyzstan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
