    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "According to the Forest Law of the Republic of Latvia adopted in 2000 (Item 2, Paragraph 3, Section 1) \"forestland is the land carrying the forest, the land under forest infrastructure facilities, as well as overflowing clearings, bogs and glades in the forest and in the territories contiguous to it\""@en .

ex:Def_def_lat_2000_898 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The forest definition is not included in Forest Act. State Land Service for land..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Latvia ;
    ex:country "Latvia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_lat_2000_898_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "The forest definition is not included in Forest Act. State Land Service for land use inventory is applying the following definition of forest and forest land: Land with tree crown cover of more than 20% and area of more than 0.1 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 7m at maturity in situ. Young natural stands and artificially reforested areas of more than 0.1 ha, up to 20 years old with mean height >1m and number of trees 2000-3000/ha (depends on species). Includes areas normally forming part of the forest area which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human intervention or natural causes but which are expected to revert to forest"@en .

