    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest - A tract of land not less than 0.1 ha, covered with trees or other forest vegetation or temporarily without it (cleared or burned areas). Not considered a forest: Clusters of trees situated in fields, by roadsides, water bodies, within towns or rural settlements as well as cemeteries, narrow - up to 10 metres - tree lines, hedges, single trees, shrubs as well as parks planted by man within towns and rural settlements"@en .

