ex:Def_def_mal_2006_597 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The areas under oil palm, rubber and tree crops are frequently regarded as fores..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Malaysia ;
    ex:country "Malaysia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "The areas under oil palm, rubber and tree crops are frequently regarded as forest. The official definition of a forest used in Malaysia differs from the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) definition, which excludes areas under agricultural crops (e.g., oil palm). (JoeangoHutan, 2006)"@en .

ex:Def_def_mal_2016_599 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The forest definition used in the development of the reference level is based on..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Malaysia ;
    ex:country "Malaysia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_mal_2016_599_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "The forest definition used in the development of the reference level is based on the national legislation and is consistent with the national greenhouse gas inventory. However, the definition used by the FAO is not used as some agricultural land, like the state land and rubber plantations would be considered as forest but these areas are not managed in a sustainable manner neither subjected by the National Forestry Act. The smallholders following the rubber management manage rubber plantations, while the state land forest is a land bank for future development. However, these areas maintain the forest threshold values Malaysia submitted under the Kyoto Protocol, a minimum area of 0.5 ha. 30% canopy cover and 5m height at maturity. The National Forest Act prescribes that only the land under this Act will remain as forest reserves and management in a sustainable manner"@en .

ex:Def_def_mal_2016_599_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_mal_unknown_1565 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The artificial establishment of forests by direct seeding or planting seedlings ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Malaysia ;
    ex:country "Malaysia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.14 STAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.1.2 Land Cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "The artificial establishment of forests by direct seeding or planting seedlings or cuttings on lands which previously (within the living memory or within 50 years) and did not carry any forests. From: hcthang@forestry.gov.my (Thang Hooi Chiew), Forestry Department Peninsular Malaysia"@en .

ex:Def_def_mal_unknown_1672 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The artificial establishment of forests by direct seeding or planting seedlings ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Malaysia ;
    ex:country "Malaysia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.4 FORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.5.1 Restoration of Land Cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "The artificial establishment of forests by direct seeding or planting seedlings or cuttings on lands which previously (within the living memory or within 50 years) carry forests. From: hcthang@forestry.gov.my (Thang Hooi Chiew), Forestry Department Peninsular Malaysia"@en .

ex:Def_def_mal_unknown_598 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An ecosystem with a minimum of 10 percent crown cover of trees and / or bamboos,..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Malaysia ;
    ex:country "Malaysia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "An ecosystem with a minimum of 10 percent crown cover of trees and / or bamboos, generally associated with wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions, and not subject to agricultural practices. This definition is also applied to the term \"forest land\". From: hcthang@forestry.gov.my (Thang Hooi Chiew), Forestry Department Peninsular Malaysia"@en .

