    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Forest land definition based on the 2000 Forest law: “A forest relates to any area larger than 0.05 ha, covered with forest trees, having a protective function, and intended for forest production or it has special purpose, no matter of tree cover and size (high forest, copice forests and other types of forest vegetation such as shrubs, shrubberies and maquis).” Also forest bare land is part of the forest land according to that definition"@en .

