ex:Def_def_nep_1988_1608 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "deforestation = reduction of stocking due to overcutting for fuelwood, timber, a..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Nepal ;
    ex:country "Nepal" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.2 DEFORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.2.2 As a change in land cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "deforestation = reduction of stocking due to overcutting for fuelwood, timber, and fodder (from Master plan for the forestry sector Nepal, main report, 1988). Krishna H Gautam <khg13@student.canterbury.ac.nz"@en .

ex:Def_def_nep_1993_284 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest land (national forests)= meant all forests, excluding private forests, wi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Nepal ;
    ex:country "Nepal" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Forest land (national forests)= meant all forests, excluding private forests, within the kingdom of Nepal, whether marked or unmarked with forest boundary markers; the term includes waste or uncultivated lands or unregistered lands surrounded by or adjoining forests, as well as paths, ponds, lakes, rivers, or streams and reverine lands with forests.(Forest Act 1993) Krishna H Gautam <khg13@student.canterbury.ac.nz"@en .

