    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "A tree-covered area greater than 5 hectares with an average canopy height of at least 6 metres and a minimum 20 percent tree crown coverage. In \"closed forests\" the trees occur in single or multiple stories with crowns interlocking.From: Indigenous Forest Policy (New Zealand Institute of Forestry, July 1998)"@en .

