    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest is Land spanning more than 0.5 ha with trees higher than 5 m and a canopy cover of more than 10%, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. Productive forest area: Forest area that under favourable stand conditions has an annual yield capacity per hectare of at least 1 cubic metre of wood including bark. Noregs Offisielle Statistikk, 1992"@en .

