    skos:note "\"Reserved Forest\" means land which was, demaracted as such at the settlement, or which may be constituted as such under the provision of the Forest Act, 1927"@en .

ex:Def_def_pak_1953_1568 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "To establish a forest on an area from which forest vegetation has always or long..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Pakistan ;
    ex:country "Pakistan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Mumtaz_Ahmad_Section_Forest_Officer_Pakistan_Min ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.14 STAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.1.2 Land Cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "To establish a forest on an area from which forest vegetation has always or long been absent. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development"@en .

ex:Def_def_pak_1953_1569 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "To establish a species or frees on an area in which it did not occur naturally. ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Pakistan ;
    ex:country "Pakistan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Mumtaz_Ahmad_Section_Forest_Officer_Pakistan_Min ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.14 STAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.1.2 Land Cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "To establish a species or frees on an area in which it did not occur naturally. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development"@en .

ex:Def_def_pak_1953_1610 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "To remove, kill or destroy all or most of the trees of a forest so that reproduc..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Pakistan ;
    ex:country "Pakistan" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Mumtaz_Ahmad_Section_Forest_Officer_Pakistan_Min ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.2 DEFORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.2.2 As a change in land cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "To remove, kill or destroy all or most of the trees of a forest so that reproduction is impossible except by artificial means. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development"@en .

ex:Def_def_pak_1953_1639 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "To remove the tree crop from a piece of land without the intention of reforestin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Pakistan ;
