    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "According to minimum tree densities which vary from species to species (as low as 90/ha for cork oak, up to 840 for most conifers) with conifer heights from 1.5-5m hand broadleaf heights from 2-5m; or where the projected area of crowns of trees more than 5m height covers more than 15% of the ground areas. This rather complicated definition is necessary to define when grant payments are applicable and is necessary because Portugal has a long agroforestry tradition. (decree 199/94) From: Gerry Lawson <gjl@ite.ac.uk"@en .

