    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Forest surface is considered the land populated by forest tree species and whose dominant canopy cover (FCC) is more than 10%. It consists of: (i) woodland - land with trees whose FCC> = 20%; (ii) sparse woodland - 10% = <FCC <20%. It also includes land with scrub or grassland species dominant plant natural expression, but a FCC of between 10% and 20%. Ministerio de Medio Ambiente y Medio Rural y Marino, 2008"@en .

