    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Land which is suitable for wood production, and not used to a significant extent for other purposes; and land where tree cover is desirable in order to protect against sand or soil erosion, or to prevent a lowering of the tree line. [Source: Swedish Forest Act"@en .

ex:Def_def_swi_1991_965 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest is defined as any area that is covered with forest trees or forest shrubs..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Switzerland ;
    ex:country "Switzerland" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest is defined as any area that is covered with forest trees or forest shrubs and can fulfil forest functions. Origin, type of use and land registry designation are not decisive. Also defined as forest are: a. grazing forests, wooded pastures and chestnut and walnut groves; b. unstocked or unproductive areas of a forest plot, such as clearings, forest roads and other forest structures and installations; c. plots subject to compulsory afforestation. Isolated groups of trees and shrubs, hedges, avenues, gardens, planted areas and parks, tree plantations established on open ground for short-term use and trees and bushes on check dams and in the immediate foreground of such installations are not defined as forest"@en .

ex:Def_def_swi_1992_303 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest Land means land including reserved forest and protected public forest. Th..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Switzerland ;
    ex:country "Switzerland" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Forest Land means land including reserved forest and protected public forest. The Forest Law"@en .

ex:Def_def_swi_1997_725 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Focuses on growing stock and applies to measurable criteria - width of forest ar..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Switzerland ;
    ex:country "Switzerland" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_swi_1997_725_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Focuses on growing stock and applies to measurable criteria - width of forest area, crown closure and top height. Width of growing stock with canopy closure = 100% is at least 25 m and with crown closure = 20% at least 50 m. Canopy closure between 20 % and 100 % depending on width of growing stock. Minimum top height 3 m (exceptions afforestation, young growth, mountain alder, mountain pine) (European Communities 1997b - p. 1067)"@en .

ex:Def_def_swi_1997_725_criteria ex:minHeight "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "25.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_swi_2006_726 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest is land covered by trees with a minimum height of 3 m and the minimum wid..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Switzerland ;
    ex:country "Switzerland" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
