    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "The Forest Act B.E. 2484 (1941) defines \"forest\" as any land which is not yet occupied by anyone according to the law. Since agricultural land and land upon which houses and other buildings are standing has presumably become private property, almost all other land except wasteland will be forest. , and"@en .

