    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "A forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10%, an area of more than 0.5 ha and an average width of more than 20 m. Trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. FOREST EUROPE, UNECE AND FAO, 2011"@en .

