    skos:note "forest reserve - An area declared to be a central forest reserve or a local forest reserve under the provision of section 4 of the FORESTS ACT, 1947. An Act To Consolidate the Law Relating to Forests and Forest Reserves"@en .

ex:Def_def_uga_1995_1614 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "When the biomass abstracted is higher than the natural growth. The Environmental..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Uganda ;
    ex:country "Uganda" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.2 DEFORESTATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.2.2 As a change in land cover" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." ;
    skos:note "When the biomass abstracted is higher than the natural growth. The Environmental Act (1995). Paolo Viskanic viskanic@imul.com"@en .

ex:Def_def_uga_2003_759 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "\"forest\" means an area of land containing a vegetation association that is predo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Uganda ;
    ex:country "Uganda" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "\"forest\" means an area of land containing a vegetation association that is predominantly composed of trees of any size, and includes - (a) a forest classified under this Act; (b) a natural forest, woodland or plantation; (c) the forest produce in a forest; and (d) the forest ecosystem; \"forest ecosystem\" means any natural or semi-natural formation of vegetation whose dominant element is trees, with closed or partially closed canopy, together with the biotic and abiotic environment; The National Forestry and Tree Planting Act, 8/2003"@en .

