    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Recent woodland (less than 400 years old), is where a wood has either been planted on an area of land, or where trees have been allowed to grow naturally through regeneration, usually as the result of a cessation in land use management"@en .

