    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "The Act creating a Protected Forest Area System in Liberia defines communal forests as “areas set aside legally or temporarily by regulation for sustainable use of forest products by local communities on a non-commercial basis”"@en .

ex:Def_def_uk_unknown_57 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Historically, a prescribed but unenclosed area of land on which the sovereign ha..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_UK ;
    ex:country "UK" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.1 General definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.1.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Historically, a prescribed but unenclosed area of land on which the sovereign had the exclusive right to hunt and make Forest Laws. More commonly, a large wooded area"@en .

ex:Def_def_uk_unknown_59 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Hunting preserve of the king or lord-marcher, subject to forest law but not nece..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_UK ;
    ex:country "UK" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.1 General definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.1.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Hunting preserve of the king or lord-marcher, subject to forest law but not necessarily woodland (L 237); originally an area of land in which only the owner had the right to hunt deer and boar"@en .

ex:Def_def_uk_unknown_60 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Its traditional definition is a territory, usually unenclosed, and not necessari..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_UK ;
    ex:country "UK" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.1 General definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.1.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Its traditional definition is a territory, usually unenclosed, and not necessarily woodland but often covered with woods of varying density, but also included heathland, wood pasture, arable and even villages. It was designated by perambulation and used by the sovereign for his or her assigned, hunting, and subject to his will by forest law. The protection of deer and their habitat was paramount. In early centuries, forest virtually meant the King’s hunting ground"@en .

ex:Def_def_uk_unknown_77 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A large area of land covered with trees and plants, usually larger than a wood, ..." ;
