    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Forest reserve - any area which has been declared as such by the King or (now) the Minister responsible for forestry. Forestry Act 1998. Via David May ISTF CVP Lesotho"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_1998_340 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest: (thorny) woodlands, protected areas including mangrove areas, urban park..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Forest: (thorny) woodlands, protected areas including mangrove areas, urban parks and trees for agricultural and commercial purposes are considered to fit the definition of forest as well. Even single trees are included in the definition if they form important esthetical elements in town or in the landscape. FAO Forestry paper 137/2, FORESTRY POLICIES IN THE CARIBEAN, volume 2: Reports of 28 selected countries and territories, FAO 1998. Facundo Franken, Department of Agriculture, Animal Production and Fisheries, Section Natural Resources Aruba"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_1998_679 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "One of main types of vegetation consist of an aggregate of trees, shrub, grassy ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "One of main types of vegetation consist of an aggregate of trees, shrub, grassy etc. plants (mosses, lichens), including animals and microorganisms biologically interconnected in the development and influencing against each other and an environment. [From: \" Russian Forest Encyclopedia\" \"Igor Yakovlev\" yakovlev@mari-el.ru Date: Sat, 6 Jun 1998 21:16:59 +0400]"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_1998_832 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Zona florestal - O espaço territorial que for reservado no plano de ordenamento ..." ;
