    skos:note "Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. FRA 2005 and 2010"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2005_1461 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Other wooded land is land with: (i) crown cover of 5–10% for trees able to reach..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2005_1461_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Other wooded land is land with: (i) crown cover of 5–10% for trees able to reach a height of 5 metres or more at maturity; or (ii) crown cover of more than 10% for trees not able to reach a height of 5 metres at maturity; or (iii) shrub or bush cover of more than 10%"@en .

