ex:Def_def_unk_2006_684 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "In the humid region forest are areas larger than 0.5 ha with tree cover more tha..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2006_684_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "In the humid region forest are areas larger than 0.5 ha with tree cover more than 20 % and trees are > 7m. In the dry region (Akagera) this is > 5m. Young forest plantation and coppices are only found in the humid area. Young forest plantation have trees less than 7 m and cover from 10- 40 % or trees more than 7 meter and cover from 10- 20 %. Bush is found in the larger humid natural forest. Tree cover is by definition less than 20 % and in practice mostly less than 10% and shrub cover more than 20 % and high forbs and grasses"@en .

