ex:Def_def_unk_2006_900 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest Land: A tract of land, including its flora and fauna, capable of producin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest Land: A tract of land, including its flora and fauna, capable of producing Forest Resources, not including land in urban areas, land in permanent settlements, and land that has been in long-term use for non-shifting cultivation of crops or livestock in a manner that precludes producing Forest Resources. An Act Adopting the National Forestry Reform Law of 2006"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2006_902 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.0625- 0.25 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20-60 Min. Tree Height ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2006_902_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.0625- 0.25 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20-60 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = 25-50 (2006). The following forest areas are not subject to the criterion of minimum stand height: shrub forest consisting of dwarf pine (Pinus mugo prostrata) and alpine alder (Alnus viridis). The following forest areas are not subject of the criteria of minimum stand height and minimum crown cover, but must have the potential to achieve both criteria: a) afforested area on land not under forest cover for 50 years (afforestations); b) regenerated forest, as well as burned, cut or damaged areas situated on land classified as forest. Although orchards, parks, camping grounds, open tree formations in settlements, gardens, cemeteries, sports and parking fields may fulfil the (quantitative) forest definition, they are not considered as forests"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2006_902_criteria ex:minHeight "0.25"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "0.25"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_2007_1315 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "\"tree\" means any woody plant regardless of its species, age or size and includes..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.4.1 Definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "\"tree\" means any woody plant regardless of its species, age or size and includes bamboo, reeds and palms as well as other plants to be designated as such by the Ministry"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2007_148 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "any area larger than one hectare (0.01 square miles) with a minimum tree cover o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
