ex:Def_def_unk_2015_506 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Guyana has elected to classify land as forest if it meets the following criteria..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2015_506_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Guyana has elected to classify land as forest if it meets the following criteria: • Tree cover of minimum 30% • Minimum height of 5 m • Minimum area of 1 ha. .It was recommended that based on Guyana’s forest characteristics, where there is largely undisturbed primary forest and the remaining being sustainably managed forests, where trees are predominantly 5 m in height, the minimum threshold for this variable is recommended to be 5m. From a monitoring perspective. The use of the upper limit (5m) would require the lowest transaction cost with no added value of going down to 2m"@en .

