    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "In Lao PDR forests are defined as areas of at least 0.5 ha in size, with crown cover above 20%; with trees that will reach higher than 5 meters when mature. Dense forests have crown cover greater than 70%, medium-stocked between 40% and 70% and degraded forests have crown cover between 20% and 40%"@en .

