    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "A stand of trees, up to 18 m in height, with an open or continuous but not thickly interlaced canopy, sometimes with shrubs interspersed, and a canopy cover of more than 20%. Grasses and herbs dominate the ground cover; epiphytic ferns are rare. Often subject to periodic burning. Woodland thicket )-defined as for bushland thicket-may also be recognized"@en .

