    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "A plant is called a tree if it has a woody stem 8 feet or more in height. The stem often has no branches for several feet above the ground. At the top it has a crown of branches and leaves. Botanists do not separate shrubs and trees. Shrubs are smaller. They branch close to the ground and have many stems. and"@en .

