    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Plants that are perennial (live for several to many years), woody (have tough cell walls of wood), shedding (use and shed woody and non-woody parts) and compartmented (made up of many compartments). Trees usually have a single stem over three yards tall. Shrubs usually have many stems less than three yards tall"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1394 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The general name of the largest of the vegetable kind, consisting of a firm wood..." ;
