    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Other wooded areas are the wooded formations of any kind less than 0,5 ha in size, as well as open woodlands having a crown density less than 20%, areas of brushwood, shrubland, stunted trees etc"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1497_criteria ex:minArea "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1498 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "This category includes natural or planted woodlots or timber tracts, cutover and..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "This category includes natural or planted woodlots or timber tracts, cutover and deforested land with young growth which has or will have value for wood products, and woodland pastured. Land covered by sagebrush or mesquite was to be reported as other pastureland and rangeland or other land. Land planted for Christmas tree production was to be reported in cropland harvested, and land in tapped maple trees reported as woodland not pastured"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_15 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The vegetation (natural or planted) or man made constructions (buildings, etc.) ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "The vegetation (natural or planted) or man made constructions (buildings, etc.) which occur on the earth surface. Water, ice, bare rock, sand and similar surfaces also count as land cover"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1500 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Wooded area - Corresponds to the FAO definition of forest and woodland. It refer..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Wooded area - Corresponds to the FAO definition of forest and woodland. It refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, and includes land from which forests have been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1501 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Woodland refers to the type of land cover characterized by trees and shrubs" ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Woodland refers to the type of land cover characterized by trees and shrubs"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1503 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Woodlands, open with less than 20% tree cover, often as small forest remnants sc..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Woodlands, open with less than 20% tree cover, often as small forest remnants scattered over the hill ranges; the domination is important: it indicates that these terrains, regardless of their administrative status, are used as grazing lands, and that their production potential for animal husbandry is more important than for timber production"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1504 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Woodlands and savannas are considered open stands of trees with crowns not usual..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1504_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.4 TREE" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Woodlands and savannas are considered open stands of trees with crowns not usually touching (generally forming 25-60% cover). Canopy tree cover may be less than 25% in cases where it exceeds shrub, herb, and nonvascular cover, respectively"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1504_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "25.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1508 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Non-forest - Land not primarily intended for growing or supporting forest. Inclu..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.6 Non-Forest" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Non-forest - Land not primarily intended for growing or supporting forest. Includes alpine, rock, slide, non-productive burn, non-productive brush, swamp or muskeg, cultivated, cleared, urban, open range, wild hay meadow, clay bank, gravel bar, and other categories"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1509 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Non-forest ecosystem - Grasslands, shrublands, chaparral, wetlands, deserts, etc..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.6 Non-Forest" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.4.4 Ecological/Miscellaneous Definitions" ;
    skos:note "Non-forest ecosystem - Grasslands, shrublands, chaparral, wetlands, deserts, etc., where trees are not the dominant life form, although they may be present as scattered individuals or in patches. See forest ecosystem. and"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_151 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1514 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The degree of occupancy of land by growing stock trees, measured by basal area a..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.11 STOCKING (Stand Density, Crown Cover)" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.9 SEMI-NATURAL FOREST See: Lund, H. Gyde. 2016 revised. Definitions of old growth, pristine, climax, ancient forests, degradation, desertification, forest fragmentation, and similar terms. [Online publication], Gainesville, VA: Forest Information Services. Misc. pagination. DOI: 10.13140/RG.2.1.2963.73612.10" ;
    skos:note "The degree of occupancy of land by growing stock trees, measured by basal area and/or the number of trees in a stand by size or age and spacing, compared to the basal area and/or number of trees required to fully utilize the growth potential of the land; that is, the stocking standard. A stocking percentage of 100 indicates full utilization of the site and is equivalent to 80 square feet of basal area per acre in trees 5.0 inches d.b.h. and larger. In a stand of trees less than 5 inches d.b.h., a stocking percentage of 100 would indicate that the present number of trees is sufficient to produce 80 square feet of basal area per acre when the trees reach 5 inches d.b.h"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1519 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stand Density - The quantity of trees per unit area, usually evaluated in terms ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.11 STOCKING (Stand Density, Crown Cover)" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.9 SEMI-NATURAL FOREST See: Lund, H. Gyde. 2016 revised. Definitions of old growth, pristine, climax, ancient forests, degradation, desertification, forest fragmentation, and similar terms. [Online publication], Gainesville, VA: Forest Information Services. Misc. pagination. DOI: 10.13140/RG.2.1.2963.73612.10" ;
    skos:note "Stand Density - The quantity of trees per unit area, usually evaluated in terms of basal area, crown cover and stocking"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1521 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "stand density [densité de peuplement (n.f.)] - A quantitative measurement of tre..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.11 STOCKING (Stand Density, Crown Cover)" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.9 SEMI-NATURAL FOREST See: Lund, H. Gyde. 2016 revised. Definitions of old growth, pristine, climax, ancient forests, degradation, desertification, forest fragmentation, and similar terms. [Online publication], Gainesville, VA: Forest Information Services. Misc. pagination. DOI: 10.13140/RG.2.1.2963.73612.10" ;
    skos:note "stand density [densité de peuplement (n.f.)] - A quantitative measurement of tree stocking, expressed in terms of number of trees, total basal area, or volume, per unit of area. More precisely, a measure of the degree of crowding of trees within a stand, commonly expressed by various growing-space ratios of crown length to tree height; crown diameter to dbh or crown diameter to tree height; or of stem spacing to tree height. (3)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1523 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking – The number and density of trees in a forest stand. Stands are often c..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.11 STOCKING (Stand Density, Crown Cover)" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.9 SEMI-NATURAL FOREST See: Lund, H. Gyde. 2016 revised. Definitions of old growth, pristine, climax, ancient forests, degradation, desertification, forest fragmentation, and similar terms. [Online publication], Gainesville, VA: Forest Information Services. Misc. pagination. DOI: 10.13140/RG.2.1.2963.73612.10" ;
    skos:note "Stocking – The number and density of trees in a forest stand. Stands are often classified as understocked, well-stocked or overstocked"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1525 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking – The relative degree of occupancy land by trees, measured as basal are..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.11 STOCKING (Stand Density, Crown Cover)" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.9 SEMI-NATURAL FOREST See: Lund, H. Gyde. 2016 revised. Definitions of old growth, pristine, climax, ancient forests, degradation, desertification, forest fragmentation, and similar terms. [Online publication], Gainesville, VA: Forest Information Services. Misc. pagination. DOI: 10.13140/RG.2.1.2963.73612.10" ;
    skos:note "Stocking – The relative degree of occupancy land by trees, measured as basal area or the number of trees in a stand by size or age and spacing, compared to the basal area or number of trees required to fully utilize the growth potential of the land; that is, the stocking standard"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1526 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking [densité relative (n.f.)] - A qualitative expression of the adequacy of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.11 STOCKING (Stand Density, Crown Cover)" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.9 SEMI-NATURAL FOREST See: Lund, H. Gyde. 2016 revised. Definitions of old growth, pristine, climax, ancient forests, degradation, desertification, forest fragmentation, and similar terms. [Online publication], Gainesville, VA: Forest Information Services. Misc. pagination. DOI: 10.13140/RG.2.1.2963.73612.10" ;
    skos:note "Stocking [densité relative (n.f.)] - A qualitative expression of the adequacy of tree cover on an area, in terms of crown closure, number of trees, basal area, or volume, in relation to a preestablished norm. In this context, \"tree cover\" includes seedlings and saplings; hence, the concept carries no connotation of a particular age. Stocking may be described in regionally or locally developed classes, or as a percentage of regional or local normal standards, which vary according to site-specific conditions. (5)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1527 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking: Degree of utilization of land by trees. Measured in terms of basal are..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.11 STOCKING (Stand Density, Crown Cover)" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.5 WOODS, WOODLAND, OTHER WOODED LANDS (OWL)." ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.9 SEMI-NATURAL FOREST See: Lund, H. Gyde. 2016 revised. Definitions of old growth, pristine, climax, ancient forests, degradation, desertification, forest fragmentation, and similar terms. [Online publication], Gainesville, VA: Forest Information Services. Misc. pagination. DOI: 10.13140/RG.2.1.2963.73612.10" ;
    skos:note "Stocking: Degree of utilization of land by trees. Measured in terms of basal area and/or the number of trees in a stand compared to the basal area and/or number of trees required to fully utilize the growth potential of the land. A stocking percent of 100 indicates full utilization of the site and is equivalent to 80 square feet of basal area per acre in trees 5 inches in dbh and larger. A stocking percent of 100 in a stand of trees less than 5 inches in dbh would indicate that the present number of trees is sufficient to produce 80 square feet of basal area per acre when the trees reach S inches dbh. A stocking percent of over 100 is fully utilizing the site. Stocking classes - Fully stocked stands -Stands in which the stocking of trees is from 100 to 133 percent. Medium stocked stands -Stands in which the stocking of trees is from 60 to 100 percent. Nonstocked areas -Commercial forest land on which the stocking of trees is less than 16.7 percent. Overstocked stands -Stands in which the stocking of trees is 133 percent or more. Poorly stocked stands -Stands in which the stocking of trees is from 16.7 to 60 percent"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1528 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The amount of live trees on a given area in relation to what is considered the o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USDA ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.11 STOCKING (Stand Density, Crown Cover)" ;
