    skos:note "Establishment and early development of new tree seedlings. In managed forests, regeneration may be natural or artificial (performed through seeding or planting.) (WESTVACO)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1716 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Devegetation - A direct human-induced long-term loss (persisting for X years or ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.6 REGENERATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.6.3 Questions:" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "Devegetation - A direct human-induced long-term loss (persisting for X years or more) of at least Y% of vegetation [characterized by cover / volume / carbon stocks] since time T on vegetation types other than forest and not subject to an elected activity under Article 3.4 of the Kyoto Protocol. Vegetation types consist of a minimum area of land of Z hectares with foliar cover of W%"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1717 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Disturbance - Any removal of tree cover sufficient to create a site for an even-..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "3.6 REGENERATION" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.6.3 Questions:" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "Disturbance - Any removal of tree cover sufficient to create a site for an even-aged crop of regeneration. Even-aged Of a forest, stand, or forest type in which relatively small age differences exist between individual trees. The differences in age permitted are usually 10 to 20 years"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1730 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "If observations are made at periods 1 and 2 and with knowledge of intended use, ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain """5.1 Illustrations 
To illustrate the difference in classification of actions on forest lands based upon the land cover or land use interpretations consider the following five examples:""" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.6.3 Questions:" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "If observations are made at periods 1 and 2 and with knowledge of intended use, the process may be called timber extraction or harvesting if human-induced, and possibly cover removal in the case of natural occurrences (fire, volcanic eruption, blowdown, etc.). The use of the label deforestation would not be appropriate, as a change in land use was not involved"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1731 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "If observations are made at periods 2 and 3, and with knowledge of intended use,..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain """5.1 Illustrations 
To illustrate the difference in classification of actions on forest lands based upon the land cover or land use interpretations consider the following five examples:""" ;
    ex:sectionSub "3.6.3 Questions:" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "If observations are made at periods 2 and 3, and with knowledge of intended use, this would be called regeneration. Reforestation may not be an appropriate term, as a change in land use was not involved"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1732 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest land would be any land used for forestry activities regardless if there w..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "5.3 Implications and Interpretations" ;
    ex:sectionSub "5.3.1 From a Land Use Interpretation - If taken literally" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "Forest land would be any land used for forestry activities regardless if there were trees present or not. Forestry activities would have to be defined. If forestry activities include soil and water protection, recreation, enhancing scenic values and wildlife habitat, then most any land capable of supporting trees would qualify including urban areas, orchards, agricultural lands"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1733 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Deforestation would be a change of land use from forestry to some other use rega..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "5.3 Implications and Interpretations" ;
    ex:sectionSub "5.3.1 From a Land Use Interpretation - If taken literally" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "Deforestation would be a change of land use from forestry to some other use regardless if the tree cover were removed or not. If protected areas, wilderness and national parks for example are not considered forestry activities, then a change of management or designation of otherwise timber producing lands to these categories would be considered deforestation even though there is not change of biomass or tree cover"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1734 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Human-induced - All changes in land use would be human induced as they are decis..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "5.3 Implications and Interpretations" ;
    ex:sectionSub "5.3.1 From a Land Use Interpretation - If taken literally" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "Human-induced - All changes in land use would be human induced as they are decisions on how the land is to be utilized"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1735 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "If change of a designation of forest land to protected, wilderness, or national ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "5.3 Implications and Interpretations" ;
    ex:sectionSub "5.3.1 From a Land Use Interpretation - If taken literally" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "If change of a designation of forest land to protected, wilderness, or national park is considered a change in land administration or use, and if change in land use is considered deforestation and if deforestation is considered an emission, then a nation may be reluctant to protect or preserve its forest resources"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1736 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Implementation - Interpretation of land cover may be done from remote sensing de..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "5.3 Implications and Interpretations" ;
    ex:sectionSub "5.3.2 From a Land Cover Interpretation - If taken literally" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "Implementation - Interpretation of land cover may be done from remote sensing depending on sensor and scale. Again, determining if change is human-induced or not may be difficult but not as difficult as determining land use"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1737 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Failing the acceptance of a land cover approach, a nation may use any definition..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological/Miscellaneous" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "5.5 Considerations" ;
    ex:sectionSub "5.3.2 From a Land Cover Interpretation - If taken literally" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" ;
    skos:note "Failing the acceptance of a land cover approach, a nation may use any definition of forest land it chooses, but would have to keep and use the same definition over the reporting periods. However, we would not be able to make country to country comparisons or analyses unless all countries used the same definition"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_174 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land on which the vegetation is dominated by forest or, if trees are lacking, th..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Land on which the vegetation is dominated by forest or, if trees are lacking, the land bears evidence of former forest and has not been converted to other vegetation. International Fund for Agricultural Development"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_176 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A minimum area of land of 0.05 – 1.0 hectares with tree crown cover (or equivale..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_176_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_IPCC ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "A minimum area of land of 0.05 – 1.0 hectares with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 – 30 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2 – 5 metres at maturity in situ. A forest may consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high portion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10 – 30 per cent or tree height of 2 – 5 metres are included under forest, as are areas normally forming part of the forest area which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human intervention such as harvesting or natural causes but which are expected to revert to forest"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_176_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_177 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest (and woodland) - Areas covered by natural or planted trees and areas that..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest (and woodland) - Areas covered by natural or planted trees and areas that are cleared but planned to be reforested. Source: - for 56 Islamic Countries"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_182 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land under natural or planted stands of trees, including land from which forest ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_United_Nations ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Land under natural or planted stands of trees, including land from which forest has been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future, and including areas occupied by roads, small cleared tracts and other small open areas within the forest"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_184 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or n..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_United_Nations ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, including land from which forest has been cleared but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future, and including areas occupied by roads, small cleared tracts and other small open areas within the forest that constitute an integral part of the forest. Includes land under coniferous and non-coniferous forest, land under mixed forest and other wooded land"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_187 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_187_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNEP ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlings under forest are also included in this class. Areas occupied by forest and woodlands with a vegetation pattern composed of native or exotic coniferous trees, and which can be used for the production of timber or other forest products. The forest trees are under normal climatic conditions higher than 5 m with a canopy closure of 30% at least"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_187_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "7.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "7.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_2 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land cover reflects the (bio) physical dimension of the earth’s surface and corr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "Land cover reflects the (bio) physical dimension of the earth’s surface and corresponds in some regard to the notion of ecosystems. Typical examples for land cover categories are built-up areas, grassland, forests or rivers and lakes"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_206 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land presently in forest, or showing evidence of having been recently under fore..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Land presently in forest, or showing evidence of having been recently under forest cover - e.g. recently clear-cut or burned and not being used for other purposes - which is expected/intended to revert to forest in the near future, either naturally or by artificial reforestation. This is because of its suitability and desirability, in view of its functions as a sustainable source of timber, as watershed protector or local climate regulator, as a shelter for macro-fauna and as biodiversity herder; the land is not currently being used for or subject to agricultural practices including planted perennial tree cropping or intensively managed grazing (FAO 19?? - IPCC)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_213 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "All land with tree cover of more than 10 % (or equivalent stocking level), or fo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_213_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "All land with tree cover of more than 10 % (or equivalent stocking level), or formerly having such tree cover and that is being naturally or artificially regenerated or that is being afforested. Land used for agricultural purposes but with 10 % or more tree cover is included. It includes coniferous and non-coniferous trees, bamboos and palms. Linear formations and planting over about 20 metres wide are also included. (Kotka-II)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_213_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_215 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forests are defined under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Cha..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_215_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "Forests are defined under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) as woody vegetation of at least 2 m in height and 10 per cent canopy cover"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_215_criteria ex:minHeight "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_216 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "This category includes all land with woody vegetation consistent with thresholds..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "This category includes all land with woody vegetation consistent with thresholds used to define forest land in the national GHG inventory, sub-divided into managed and unmanaged, and also by ecosystem type as specified in the IPCC Guidelines*. It also includes systems with vegetation that currently fall below, but are expected to exceed, the threshold of the forest land category. (See Marrakesh definition of forest)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_217 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A canopy cover of at least 40 percent by woody plants taller than 5 meters. The ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_217_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_United_Nations ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.2 International definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.2.3 As a land use type" ;
    skos:note "A canopy cover of at least 40 percent by woody plants taller than 5 meters. The existence of many other definitions is acknowledged, and other limits (such as crown cover greater than 10 percent, as used by the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations) will also be reported. Includes temporarily cut-over forests and plantations; excludes orchards and agroforests where the main products are food crops"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_217_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_232 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Le domaine forestier de l'Etat comprend : - les réserves naturelles intégrales, ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:region "Africa" ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Le domaine forestier de l'Etat comprend : - les réserves naturelles intégrales, - les parcs nationaux, - les réserves de faune, - les forêts récréatives, - les périmètres de protection, - les périmètres de reboisement et - les forêts de production. Loi Nº 90.003 Portant Code Forestier Centrafricain"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_234 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "State Forest: State land declared as forest according to the Forest Law disregar..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "State Forest: State land declared as forest according to the Forest Law disregarding whether there is any vegetation on that land or not. A.K. Christou \"Forestry Department - Research and Publicity Sector\""@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_24 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The social and economic purposes for which land is managed (e.g., grazing, timbe..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_IPCC ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "The social and economic purposes for which land is managed (e.g., grazing, timber extraction, conservation). and"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_25 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land use is based on the functional dimension of land for different human purpos..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "Land use is based on the functional dimension of land for different human purposes or economic activities. Typical categories for land use are dwellings, industrial use, transport, recreational use or nature protection areas"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_26 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The total of arrangements, activities and inputs undertaken in a certain land co..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNEP ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "The total of arrangements, activities and inputs undertaken in a certain land cover type (a set of human actions). The social and economic purposes for which land is managed (e.g., grazing, timber extraction, and conservation)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_265 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "2. Land which was declared as Forest Land by any legal or official program or 3...." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "2. Land which was declared as Forest Land by any legal or official program or 3. Land managed by the Israeli Forest Department. From: GilS@kkl.org.il"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_3 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land cover can simply be defined as \"the physical attributes of the land that ca..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNEP ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "Land cover can simply be defined as \"the physical attributes of the land that can be seen readily as opposed to the land use which describes a pattern of human activities undertaken within a social and economic context\""@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_301 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An area of land, with or without trees, declared to be a forest reserve, protect..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "An area of land, with or without trees, declared to be a forest reserve, protected forest, or prohibited area (Source: Michael Andrew, chiefforest@maffe.org)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_302 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Government forest reserves managed by the forest department. It can be bare land..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Government forest reserves managed by the forest department. It can be bare land intended to be planted with trees or shrubs in the future (K. H. Badi, Forest Deptartment, Sudan A. M.S. Bayoumi, Forest Department, Sudan)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_313 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every part of a forest declared..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.1 As a declared, legal, or administrative unit" ;
    skos:note "Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every part of a forest declared to be a Forest Reserve under the Land Regulations for the time being in force – Forest Act: Chapter 66:01. Narine Lackhan, Director of Forestry"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_335 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Includes: upland forests, coastal forests, mangrove forests, dwarf forests, moss..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.3 FOREST/FOREST LAND" ;
    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "Includes: upland forests, coastal forests, mangrove forests, dwarf forests, moss forests, secondary vegetations and agroforest areas (including ones with coconuts and bananas)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_34 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land \"use\" is defined in terms of a specific combination of land activity and la..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "Land \"use\" is defined in terms of a specific combination of land activity and land cover"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_35 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land use is characterized by the arrangements, activities and inputs people unde..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "Land use is characterized by the arrangements, activities and inputs people undertake in a certain land cover type to produce, change or maintain it. The definition of land use establishes a direct link between land cover and the actions of people in their environment"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_37 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The current use of an area of land. This term is different to, but often confuse..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "The current use of an area of land. This term is different to, but often confused with, land cover"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_38 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The description of human enterprises on the land and water, and may have the fol..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    ex:sectionMain "2.1 LAND COVER" ;
    skos:note "The description of human enterprises on the land and water, and may have the following components: activities (the actual use of land and related structures and modifications to the landscape); use-related land cover (where cover implies a use or is important to interpreting patterns or impacts of use); declared interests in the land (where use decisions may be affected by such interests); legal entities (legal boundaries, tenures, and regulations that affect use)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_42 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Table 1 lists terms for forest, forestland and tree in a multitude of languages ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Unknown ;
