    ex:sectionSub "2.3.3 National definitions" ;
    ex:sectionSubSub "2.3.3.2 As a land cover type" ;
    skos:note "(Local Arabic term for Forests: Ghabat or Ahraj) - Piece of land covered a vegetation in which trees (not only fruit trees) are predominant(over 50%), and with at least 3 ha of continuously forested area, and with a tree crown cover equal or superior to 10%. Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com"@en .

